# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type }})

> **Business Edition only.** This endpoint does not exist in Portainer CE.

The `portainer_addon_repair` action reissues the credential an installed addon authenticates to Portainer with. Run it when an addon reports `health_status = "credential-invalid"`.

> **Requirements:** Terraform >= 1.14 (actions). OpenTofu does not support actions; there, and with older Terraform, use the [`portainer_addon_repair` resource](../resources/addon_repair.md), which runs the same operation when it is created.

## Example Usage

### Run it from a lifecycle `action_trigger`

```hcl
action "portainer_addon_repair" "portal" {
  config {
    addon_id = "portal-template"
  }
}

resource "terraform_data" "portal_credential" {
  input = var.portal_credential_rotation

  lifecycle {
    action_trigger {
      events  = [after_update]
      actions = [action.portainer_addon_repair.portal]
    }
  }
}
```

### Run it on demand

```shell
terraform apply -invoke action.portainer_addon_repair.portal
```

## Lifecycle & Behavior

- The action runs only when it is invoked: from an `action_trigger` on the events listed there, or with `terraform apply -invoke`. A plan lists the invocations it would run; nothing is stored in state, so there is nothing to destroy and no `triggers` argument is needed to run it again.
- It sends the same requests as the `portainer_addon_repair` resource does when it is created, with the same defaults, and fails the apply with the same errors.
- The addon state Portainer reports after the repair is not returned: actions have no attributes. Read it with the `portainer_addons` data source.

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Attributes Reference

Actions have no attributes: nothing they return can be referenced elsewhere in the configuration.
